ds of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":229662,"global_rank":113212,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19618},{"name":"richford/hbn_url_csv","owner":"richford","html_url":"https://github.com/richford/hbn_url_csv","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229659,"global_rank":113215,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19619},{"name":"dilraj45/nary-search","owner":"dilraj45","html_url":"https://github.com/dilraj45/nary-search","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":3,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229634,"global_rank":113246,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19620},{"name":"indrajeet95/Computer-Networking-and-Internet-Technologies","owner":"indrajeet95","html_url":"https://github.com/indrajeet95/Computer-Networking-and-Internet-Technologies","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229631,"global_rank":113248,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19621},{"name":"spiceai/tableau-connector","owner":"spiceai","html_url":"https://github.com/spiceai/tableau-connector","stars":0,"forks":2,"watchers":0,"issues":5,"language":"Python","description":"Spice.ai Tableau Connector","topics":[],"score":229626,"global_rank":113258,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19622},{"name":"kevinslin/dotfiles"